# Secrets. Atmos.Api.csproj copies appsettings*.yaml to the publish output, and that
# glob matches the development file - which is where real client secrets live. It is
# gitignored, so a clean checkout has none, but `docker build .` reads the working
# tree rather than the index. Excluded here so a local build cannot bake one in.
**/appsettings.Development.yaml
**/appsettings.development.yaml

# Build output. Beyond size, host artefacts from a different OS and architecture
# have no business in a Linux build.
**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/

# Not part of the API image
tests/
src/Atmos.AppHost/
.local-media/

# Tooling, history and editor state
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
.claude/
.superpowers/
docs/
**/*.user
**/*.DotSettings
**/*.DotSettings.user

# Not read by the build
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
LICENSE
Atmos.slnx
